(2613907, 358281, 61191, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments!! I''m very happy with this first submission to a challenge. Ok, there was a dnmc-problem: my dictionary told me, that "stationery" means something like "all kind of paper". But when the voting began, I knew what "stationery" really stands for...</td>', 'Thanks for your comments!! I''m very happy with this first submission to a challenge. Ok, there was a dnmc-problem: my dictionary told me, that "stationery" means something like "all kind of paper". But when the voting began, I knew what "stationery" really stands for...', '2006-07-12 07:14:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(2613912, 357103, 57229, '<td valign="top">It was you, ya rat - and I gave you all my invective frustrations and a 2, after all those not only nice but also perceptive comments you sent my way.<br/> <br/>I still rate gratuitous nudity/binties as no better than gratuitous insects and flowers.<br/> <br/>Erm - no - gratuitious nudity is better than gratuitous flowers.<br/> <br/>Mind you, I have also at this altogether too late stage spotted that indeed it isn''t gratuitous and that I - duh - didn''t get it.<br/> <br/>Well, at least I put my hand up to be counted.<br/> <br/>Will try harder.<br/> <br/>FWIW, a bit of decentralisation of subject(s) - model out to the right a bit, window out to the left... I could sort of see the letter being on something, but then you''d lose the barren thing... I assume that''s a <i>softwood</i> floor, but that''s good, because it needs a covering and doesn''t have one.<br/> <br/>Anyway, sorry, next time I''ll give you a three.</td>', 'It was you, ya rat - and I gave you all my invective frustrations and a 2, after all those not only nice but also perceptive comments you sent my way. I still rate gratuitous nudity/binties as no better than gratuitous insects and flowers. Erm - no - gratuitious nudity is better than gratuitous flowers. Mind you, I have also at this altogether too late stage spotted that indeed it isn''t gratuitous and that I - duh - didn''t get it. Well, at least I put my hand up to be counted. Will try harder. FWIW, a bit of decentralisation of subject(s) - model out to the right a bit, window out to the left... I could sort of see the letter being on something, but then you''d lose the barren thing... I assume that''s a softwood floor, but that''s good, because it needs a covering and doesn''t have one. Anyway, sorry, next time I''ll give you a three.', '2006-07-12 07:22:03.000000', NULL, 0),
