(2614544, 357809, 20530, '<td valign="top">I''m thinking the low scores come from those who didn''t make the connection  to stationery. I didn''t vote this challenge; but upon opening this image, my first thought was that it was a well lit shot of something you purchased.<br/> <br/>After reading about your set-up, I''m completely impressed. It seems apparent that you are the victim of "too much creativity". Hopefully this talent is more rewarding than a few votes from strangers on the internet. I see a definite trend in well thought out and unique images in your portfolio.<br/> <br/>Can''t wait to see what you come up with next!<br/></td>', 'I''m thinking the low scores come from those who didn''t make the connection  to stationery. I didn''t vote this challenge; but upon opening this image, my first thought was that it was a well lit shot of something you purchased. After reading about your set-up, I''m completely impressed. It seems apparent that you are the victim of "too much creativity". Hopefully this talent is more rewarding than a few votes from strangers on the internet. I see a definite trend in well thought out and unique images in your portfolio. Can''t wait to see what you come up with next!', '2006-07-12 12:05:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2614608, 358311, 58999, '<td valign="top">kteach: I fully agree with your observations. The finger does get lost in the paper. About the color: reducing the yellow was making the hand look like actual skin color and was not producing the ancient feel, but I agree that I need to learn sepia toning. This was my first attempt at making sepia.<br/> <br/>lauralink: Yeah, it doesn''t look ancient to me as well :) an older hand, and a better burning (not photoshop burning, but burning in oven) of the paper could have made it look ancient.<br/> <br/>Commando303: You have it right.<br/> <br/>Jutilda: I fully agree with you. It does need more negative space and a different angle.<br/> <br/>once again, thanks every one for your excellent remarks.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-12 12:15:02.</i></td>', 'kteach: I fully agree with your observations. The finger does get lost in the paper. About the color: reducing the yellow was making the hand look like actual skin color and was not producing the ancient feel, but I agree that I need to learn sepia toning. This was my first attempt at making sepia. lauralink: Yeah, it doesn''t look ancient to me as well :) an older hand, and a better burning (not photoshop burning, but burning in oven) of the paper could have made it look ancient. Commando303: You have it right. Jutilda: I fully agree with you. It does need more negative space and a different angle. once again, thanks every one for your excellent remarks.', '2006-07-12 12:26:30.000000', '2006-07-12 13:15:02.000000', 0),
(2614613, 358403, 57358, '<td valign="top">Oh sweet!!  now it''s on....!!  J/K.. well, only a little, lol<br/> <br/>Congratulations, I saw this, but didn''t even think to look at who it was, man, look who gave who a run for their money now.....<br/> <br/>and ha HA, I see that I don''t need to feel so guilty for ditching my minolta so much anymore</td>', 'Oh sweet!!  now it''s on....!!  J/K.. well, only a little, lol Congratulations, I saw this, but didn''t even think to look at who it was, man, look who gave who a run for their money now..... and ha HA, I see that I don''t need to feel so guilty for ditching my minolta so much anymore', '2006-07-12 12:27:42.000000', NULL, 0),
