(2616447, 358642, 56658, '<td valign="top">Being a huge fan of body art myself I see where you are going with this and I like it. Tattos on many people tell more storys of their life than paper ever will.<br/> <br/>The hip does look a little strange in that position but otherwise I think it is very good. I would say it is a pretty good score for being so out of the box but then again it is a semi nude:) good job.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-12 20:06:05.</i></td>', 'Being a huge fan of body art myself I see where you are going with this and I like it. Tattos on many people tell more storys of their life than paper ever will. The hip does look a little strange in that position but otherwise I think it is very good. I would say it is a pretty good score for being so out of the box but then again it is a semi nude:) good job.', '2006-07-12 21:03:55.000000', '2006-07-12 21:06:05.000000', 0),
(2616528, 357809, 22975, '<td valign="top">i think i would have voted your entry higher had i seen it presented in lighting like the prop photo.  i gave you a 5, because i, too, thought it was one of those fold out crepe thingies you get a party stores, so just like i would likely vote most statues or pictures of other crafty objects in other challenges, i thought it was sort of ho-hum.  i felt you met the challenge because even though it may have been a crepe thing, it was still paper, which is all stationery in my book.  it''s a gorgeous work of art made with paper... i have a new respect for it now, but... and this is just my little ol'' opinion, i wasn''t a fan of the lighting or the composition... so with all of those things, that''s why i gave you a 5.</td>', 'i think i would have voted your entry higher had i seen it presented in lighting like the prop photo.  i gave you a 5, because i, too, thought it was one of those fold out crepe thingies you get a party stores, so just like i would likely vote most statues or pictures of other crafty objects in other challenges, i thought it was sort of ho-hum.  i felt you met the challenge because even though it may have been a crepe thing, it was still paper, which is all stationery in my book.  it''s a gorgeous work of art made with paper... i have a new respect for it now, but... and this is just my little ol'' opinion, i wasn''t a fan of the lighting or the composition... so with all of those things, that''s why i gave you a 5.', '2006-07-12 21:25:18.000000', NULL, 0),
