(2640169, 357437, 20530, '<td valign="top">First of all; let me say that I checked out your portfolio when this challenge was over and was thoroughly impressed with your success right out of the gate. It''s obvious that you are very talented; and I predict that you are going to continue submitting unusual and interesting images for our enjoyment.<br/> <br/>The first thing that struck me about this image was how the title enhances it. The "diary" is animated, and indeed, appears to be flying. On it''s own, it might not be that captivating; however, the sunrise in BG and reflecting from the pages really adds the color and warmth that makes this image "pop". DOF, focus...everything is spot-on.<br/> <br/>If I had to think of a nitpick, I guess it would be the finger at the left. Honestly though, I didn''t even see it until I had been looking for a very long time.<br/> <br/>Excellent work. And congratulations on your ribbon! I''m envious:)</td>', 'First of all; let me say that I checked out your portfolio when this challenge was over and was thoroughly impressed with your success right out of the gate. It''s obvious that you are very talented; and I predict that you are going to continue submitting unusual and interesting images for our enjoyment. The first thing that struck me about this image was how the title enhances it. The "diary" is animated, and indeed, appears to be flying. On it''s own, it might not be that captivating; however, the sunrise in BG and reflecting from the pages really adds the color and warmth that makes this image "pop". DOF, focus...everything is spot-on. If I had to think of a nitpick, I guess it would be the finger at the left. Honestly though, I didn''t even see it until I had been looking for a very long time. Excellent work. And congratulations on your ribbon! I''m envious:)', '2006-07-19 22:28:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2641329, 356980, 17148, '<td valign="top">You have been registered since December and this is your first challenge...shame on you...only kidd''n...shoot more...it''s fun.</td>', 'You have been registered since December and this is your first challenge...shame on you...only kidd''n...shoot more...it''s fun.', '2006-07-20 04:22:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(2653753, 358048, 61336, '<td valign="top">Just came back from a 15 day camping (no phone, no electricity) and saw the results today. Actually... better than i expected.<br/>Thank you all for the votes and comments.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-07-25 02:29:22.</i></td>', 'Just came back from a 15 day camping (no phone, no electricity) and saw the results today. Actually... better than i expected.Thank you all for the votes and comments.', '2006-07-24 04:29:45.000000', '2006-07-25 03:29:22.000000', 0),
(2659617, 356780, 14614, '<td valign="top">risky one here.  The use of words/letters draws my eye to them (just the stuff on the bottom of the page) and I''m left struggling between reading and taking in the frame.    I''m all around the frame - if I image the frame with the writing blurred or in characters I can''t interpret, I get more of a sense of lines and angles with lots of gray.  Feel the flat lighting was the way to go but it doesn''t add any interest.</td>', 'risky one here.  The use of words/letters draws my eye to them (just the stuff on the bottom of the page) and I''m left struggling between reading and taking in the frame.    I''m all around the frame - if I image the frame with the writing blurred or in characters I can''t interpret, I get more of a sense of lines and angles with lots of gray.  Feel the flat lighting was the way to go but it doesn''t add any interest.', '2006-07-25 19:41:51.000000', NULL, 0),
